ive yourself and  move on  no on the other hand if you're that type  of person like me  that always has a back-up plan for a  back-up plan it's not necessarily a bad  thing  you just need to be able to control it  better let me explain what i mean here  you need to learn how to plan really  good without worrying or stressing about  the outcome about the results  so you need to understand there's a  difference between overthinking and  planning really good planning for things  that might happen let me explain if you  think about all the possibilities of  what might happen  you can plan for the unexpected and be  ready for anything  and listen you have to plan for the  future because if you don't plan for the  future you are planning to fail so plan  for the future have your backup plans be  ready for anything  but then  once you did your best you gave it your  all 100 to plan don't worry about the  outcome because you cannot control the  outcome  even if the outcome is bad you can still  be happy with yourself because then you  know man  i've tried my best i couldn't have done  anything different and you know it's  never about the destination that makes  life so interesting it's all about the  journey because it's on the journey  where you grow and where you learn  that's where you actually have the most  fun  and if you fail it's not the end of the  world when you fall you just get back up  again if you fall again you get back up  again  just take it one day at a time and don't  over complicate things martin luther  king jr said  if you can't fly then run  if you can't run then walk  if you can't walk then crawl  but by all means keep moving  and here's the thing if you're still  young you need to understand that you  will probably fail many times in your  life  that's gonna happen  that is what it means to be a human you  will make mistakes  and then all that you do is just you get  up again that's it  the worst thing you can do is to not  stand up again because if